  '''
  Plan for the onboarding of example-org/infra at <tmp>/repo
    1. EXEC the Ansible config of <tmp>/repo
         <tmp>/user-data/tools/ansible-core/2.22.0/bin/ansible-config dump --format json --only-changed  [only if an Ansible tool environment is installed]
    2. EXEC the Ansible inventory of <tmp>/repo
         <tmp>/user-data/tools/ansible-core/2.22.0/bin/ansible-inventory -i '<inventory>' --list  [only if an Ansible tool environment is installed and the project profile names an inventory]
    3. EXEC the host key of <host> in known_hosts
         ssh-keygen -F '<host>' -f <tmp>/home/.ssh/known_hosts  [only if <tmp>/home/.ssh/known_hosts exists]  [repeated for each host in service]
    4. EXEC the kubeconfig contexts
         kubectl config get-contexts -o name
    5. WRITE infra.repos in <tmp>/.test_config/config.yaml
  The command also reads the files of the checkout and the devops ssh key folder.
  
  '''
